<title>Video.width Function</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
i = video_name.width();
</logicsyntax>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <logiccolor>Video.width</logiccolor> function returns the display width, in pixels, of the video held by the <link Video.csdoc>Video</link> object.

The <logiccolor>Video.width</logiccolor> function only supports video recorded in the format that CSPro uses to create recordings: <link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebM">WebM</link>. The function will return <logiccolor>default</logiccolor> for non-WebM video files.


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

The function returns the width in pixels, or <logiccolor>default</logiccolor> if the Video object does not contain a video or if the width cannot be computed.


